<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oswulf of Northumbria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 759</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oswulf was king of Northumbria from 758 to 759, the son of King Eadberht, who abdicated in his favour to become a monk at York. Within a year, on 24 July 759, he was murdered by members of his own household. His death opened a period of rapid turnover in which several Northumbrian kings were deposed or killed.</p></div>
